question_description:
On October 7, 2023, [Hamas launched an attack on Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Al-Aqsa_Flood), with [reports](https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/16/middleeast/israel-hamas-gaza-war-explained-week-2-mime-intl/index.html) stating that more than 1,400 Israeli civilians were killed. Israel almost immediately began striking targets in Gaza and then moved ground forces into Gaza in late October, with the [stated goal of wiping out Hamas](https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-67084141).&#x20;

After more than a year of very intense fighting, Gaza lay in ruins with more than 50,000 Palestinian deaths and 1,200 Israeli deaths, according to the [United Nations](https://www.ochaopt.org/content/reported-impact-snapshot-gaza-strip-30-april-2025). The two sides [agreed to a ceasefire](https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-hamas-war-news-05-05-2025-d22caabfd2cf89e83fe06e649e6438ba) in January 2025, which lasted through mid-March. Since the end of the ceasefire through the time of this question, Israel has recaptured territory from Hamas and now controls 50% of the Gaza Strip.&#x20;

On May 5, 2025, Israel's security cabinet [approved](https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/05/middleeast/israel-gaza-expansion-hnk-intl) a large expansion of Israel's military operations in Gaza, involving the call-up of tens of thousands of reservists, with the intention of moving substantially all of the Gazan civilian population to the southern part of the Gaza Strip (south of Gaza City) and possibly even annexing part of the territory, with Finance Minister Bezalel Smotrich saying, "we are finally going to conquer the Gaza Strip."

In addition to the possibility of Israel itself controlling and governing Gaza City if it captures it from Hamas, other options reported to be considered for governing the area are the [Palestinian Authority](https://www.timesofisrael.com/abbas-pa-ready-to-assume-full-responsibility-in-gaza-strip-when-ceasefire-begins/) and an [international peacekeeping force](https://www.timesofisrael.com/biden-administration-said-to-weigh-us-led-gaza-peacekeeping-force-after-war-ends/).&#x20;
